\c 1
\s1 A Greeting from the Elder
\r (\ref 2 John 1:1–3|2JN 1-3\ref*)
\p \v 1 The elder,
\p To the beloved Gaius, whom I love in \add the\add* truth:
\p \v 2 Beloved, I pray that in every way you may prosper and enjoy good health, as your soul \add also\add* prospers. \v 3 For I was overjoyed \add when the\add* brothers came and testified about your devotion to the truth, in \add which\add* you continue to walk. \v 4 I have no greater joy than to hear \add that\add* my children are walking in the truth.
\s1 Gaius Commended for Hospitality
\p \v 5 Beloved, you are faithful in what you are doing for the brothers, and \add especially since\add* they are strangers \add to you\add*. \v 6 \add They\add* have testified to \add the\add* church about your love. You will do well to send them on their way in a manner worthy of God. \v 7 For they went out on behalf of the Name, accepting nothing from the Gentiles. \v 8 Therefore we ought to support such \add men\add*, so that we may be fellow workers for the truth.
\s1 Diotrephes and Demetrius
\p \v 9 I have written to the church \add about this\add*,\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Literally \fqa I have written something to the church\f* but Diotrephes, who loves to be first, will not accept our \add instruction\add*. \v 10 So if I come, I will call attention to \add his\add* malicious slander \add against\add* us. And unsatisfied with that, he refuses to welcome the brothers and forbids those who want to do so, even putting \add them\add* out of the church.
\p \v 11 Beloved, \add do\add* not imitate what \add is\add* evil, but what \add is\add* good. The \add one who\add* does good is of God; the \add one who\add* does evil has not seen God.
\p \v 12 Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone, and from the truth itself. We also testify \add for him\add*, and you know that our testimony is true.
\s1 Conclusion
\r (\ref 2 John 1:12–13|2JN 12-13\ref*)
\p \v 13 I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not \add to do so\add* with pen and ink. \v 14 Instead, I hope to see you soon and speak \add with you face\add* to \add face\add*.\f + \fr 1:14 \ft Literally \fqa and we will speak mouth to mouth\ft ; some translators begin a new verse (15) after \fqa face to face.\f*
\p Peace to you.
\p The friends \add here \add* send you greetings.
\p Greet \add each of our\add* friends \add there\add* by name.
